      "reply": "I read the glossary in the task workdir (`GLOSSARY.md`); the repo has only one glossary and no `GLOSSARY-MAP.md`, so I used its terms: **Graph**, **Node**, **Checkpoint**.\n\n---\n\n**Context**\n\nYou asked how the task continues after you approve it.\n\n**Re-pitch**\n\n- The Graph stops at a confirmation boundary. It waits there.\n- The Graph saves a Checkpoint. The Checkpoint ties your reply to the execution that is now suspended.\n- The next Node in the Graph produces the report. It does this after the suspended execution starts again.\n- The Checkpoint does not guarantee that an external file write happens only one time. This is the case if the task stops unexpectedly, for example after a crash.\n\n**Note on the terms**\n\n- *Checkpoint* means a saved record of the Graph state that can help it continue.\n- The last point is a limit, not a fault. The Graph can continue, but you must not rely on the Checkpoint to prevent a repeated write to an external file.",
